  "result": "The fix is in `src/server/repositories/_paging.ts`. Type-checking passes, and all 617 tests pass (73 files). No existing test covers the case of many entries sharing one timestamp.\n\n**Cause:** \"Load more\" resumed after the last entry shown by asking only for entries with an earlier timestamp. Bulk actions record many entries at the same moment, so the rest of that batch got skipped.\n\n**Fix:** `keysetPredicate` now also uses the entry's id to break ties, matching the order the lists are already sorted in. It now resumes with \"earlier timestamp, or same timestamp and a smaller id\". Every list that uses this helper gets the fix: issues, notifications, audit log, comments, members, projects and search. The workspace filter is still applied to every page, so other workspaces' entries stay excluded.\n\nSeparately, the claude.ai Gmail and Google Drive connectors need to be authorized in your claude.ai connector settings before they can be used.",
